// A refusal the parser cannot yet tell is needed: a construct inside, or in the
// signature of, a function that nothing may call, which is common in a header
// (a `static inline` helper using a typeof whose operand is a local). It is kept
// with the external declaration being read; when that declaration ends it is
// kept for the function it turned out to define (told by the check pass only if
// the function is reached), or told at once when the declaration defines none.
